  "name": "WARFARIN THERAPEUTIC RESPONSE PREDICTIVE ASSAY (VKORC1 & CYP2C9)",
  "code": "2529",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1986\" data-end=\"2193\">\n<p data-start=\"1988\" data-end=\"2043\">High Sensitivity (VKORC1 AA and/or CYP2C9&nbsp;<em data-start=\"2032\" data-end=\"2041\">2/<em data-start=\"2035\" data-end=\"2040\">3):</em></em></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2046\" data-end=\"2193\">\n<li data-start=\"2046\" data-end=\"2108\">\n<p data-start=\"2048\" data-end=\"2108\"><strong data-start=\"2048\" data-end=\"2083\">Greatly increased bleeding risk</strong> if standard dose used.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2111\" data-end=\"2193\">\n<p data-start=\"2113\" data-end=\"2193\">Initiate with <strong data-start=\"2127\" data-end=\"2162\">lower dose (often 0.5&ndash;3 mg/day)</strong> and frequent INR monitoring.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2195\" data-end=\"2338\">\n<p data-start=\"2197\" data-end=\"2263\"><strong data-start=\"2197\" data-end=\"2261\">Intermediate Sensitivity (VKORC1 GA or CYP2C9 heterozygous):</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2266\" data-end=\"2338\">\n<li data-start=\"2266\" data-end=\"2338\">\n<p data-start=\"2268\" data-end=\"2338\">Requires <strong data-start=\"2277\" data-end=\"2298\">25&ndash;50% lower dose</strong> than standard (typically 2&ndash;5 mg/day).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2340\" data-end=\"2456\">\n<p data-start=\"2342\" data-end=\"2396\">Normal Sensitivity (VKORC1 GG and CYP2C9&nbsp;<em data-start=\"2385\" data-end=\"2394\">1/<em data-start=\"2388\" data-end=\"2393\">1):</em></em></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2399\" data-end=\"2456\">\n<li data-start=\"2399\" data-end=\"2456\">\n<p data-start=\"2401\" data-end=\"2456\">Standard dose (5&ndash;7 mg/day) with routine INR monitoring.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2458\" data-end=\"2573\">\n<p data-start=\"2460\" data-end=\"2573\">Must be used <strong data-start=\"2473\" data-end=\"2554\">alongside INR testing and clinical factors (age, diet, weight, comorbidities)</strong> for safe dosing.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
